+The advanced lane is reported as engineered intelligence rather than as an opaque model handle. At a high level, EI does four things: it searches for complementary detector-score families on train/CV rows, combines them with a sparse nonnegative late-fusion weight vector, calibrates the fused score with a monotone geodesic-odds map, and writes a selection lock before the blind holdout is scored. It does not tune on holdout rows, use hidden generator metadata, or claim measured-platform truth.
+
+This explanation matters because a post-hoc view control can be strong on one metric without being the locked candidate. In this run, the passive-RF-only view has higher AP and swept Recall@$\leq$1\%FPR than the full EI candidate, but its selected-threshold F1 and ECE are worse. We therefore report EI as the locked, calibrated selected-threshold artifact, not as a universal dominator of every view control.
