+\subsection{Hard-negative taxonomy}
+Hard negatives are modeled to stress low-FPR behavior rather than to estimate field rates. Bird families include single bird, flock aggregate, shorebird/wader, gull/tern, raptor/falcon, flamingo/large bird, seabird/cormorant, and seasonal migratory density. RC fixed-wing aircraft are modeled as benign propeller-driven hard negatives with speed/aspect/cadence overlap. Weather cells, ground vehicles, wind turbines, multipath ghosts, RFI bursts, terrain glint, and clutter-only counterfactuals are separate non-target stressors.
+
+\subsection{Validation boundary}
+The evidence bundle records leakage diagnostics, label-shuffle sanity, metadata-only and stratum-only baselines, nearest-neighbor train/holdout scans, selected-threshold confusion matrices, fixed-FPR recall, calibration, and group-block bootstrap intervals. These are audit artifacts. They do not convert the synthetic corpus into measured truth, and they do not provide track-level operational false-alarm rate.
+
+\subsection{Prohibited inferences}
+The following interpretations are prohibited: measured Iranian-drone radar signature, operational route behavior, evasion or countermeasure optimization, payload-effects inference, fielded-sensor performance, vendor-equivalent signal processing, classified-fidelity claim, track-level FAR claim, or deployment-performance claim.
